["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Self-evolving AI could close the loop in six months, but the model will quietly drift The inflection point for RSI is models becoming capable of long-horizon tasks. Apodex&#x27;s chief scientist says the self-evolution loop could close in as little as six months, but recursive drift and the model&#x27;s taste will need human gatekeeping for a long time yet. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E242｜最快半年AI跑通自进化？与陈天桥首席科学家聊聊硅谷模型必争之地 AI self-evolution RSI Long-horizon tasks Agent teams Model taste Research automation RSI (Recursive Self-Improvement) Recursive Drift Heavy Duty Solver Discovery Model Agent Team\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-06-sv101-ai最快半年跑通自进化-验证与品味是最后门槛/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/f/f0f20376-8faf-4940-b920-84af6c734e2d/cover.jpg?v=6\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">1:10:54</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0706</span></div>\n<h2>Self-evolving AI could close the loop in six months, but the model will quietly drift</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The inflection point for RSI is models becoming capable of long-horizon tasks. Apodex&#x27;s chief scientist says the self-evolution loop could close in as little as six months, but recursive drift and the model&#x27;s taste will need human gatekeeping for a long time yet.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI self-evolution</span><span class=\"tag\">RSI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"The narcissism epidemic is media hype: the data doesn&#x27;t support it, and narcissists themselves suffer more The much-hyped ‘narcissism epidemic’ has little data behind it; narcissism as measured by the NPI has actually been falling in recent years. True NPD affects about 1%, patients often carry depression and anxiety alongside it, and treatment works but takes years. Science Vs Science Vs Narcissists: Are We Surrounded? Narcissism NPD Personality disorders Psychotherapy Workplace relationships Science communication NPI (Narcissistic Personality Inventory) NPD (Narcissistic Personality Disorder) Grandiose narcissism Gray rocking Empathy prompt Triple E\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-02-sciencevs-没有自恋流行病-自恋者只是更痛苦/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/f521b120-2c30-11e6-b5f3-63ee984ee1a4/image/e7470287efbfa0aff068175bb6c31805.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">44:38</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0702</span></div>\n<h2>The narcissism epidemic is media hype: the data doesn&#x27;t support it, and narcissists themselves suffer more</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The much-hyped ‘narcissism epidemic’ has little data behind it; narcissism as measured by the NPI has actually been falling in recent years. True NPD affects about 1%, patients often carry depression and anxiety alongside it, and treatment works but takes years.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Narcissism</span><span class=\"tag\">NPD</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Mathematicians Become Curators; the Value Is Not in the Proof AI can solve problems, explain them, and prove theorems; the mathematician&#x27;s value shifts toward judging which path is worth taking — and toward being a curator people trust. Dwarkesh Podcast Dwarkesh Grant Sanderson – AI and the future of math Mathematics AI capability limits Verifiability Curation Learning grindability theory of mind RLVR Langlands Program\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-30-dwarkesh-数学家未来是策展人-价值不在证明里/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://apple.dwarkesh-podcast.workers.dev/art/v1/c3Vic3RhY2s6cG9zdDoyMDQyNzU5MTY.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:33:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Dwarkesh Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0630</span></div>\n<h2>Mathematicians Become Curators; the Value Is Not in the Proof</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI can solve problems, explain them, and prove theorems; the mathematician&#x27;s value shifts toward judging which path is worth taking — and toward being a curator people trust.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Mathematics</span><span class=\"tag\">AI capability limits</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s next breakthrough isn&#x27;t training — it&#x27;s letting AI learn on the job The labs are betting RLVR will generalize into general intelligence, but the real bottlenecks are sample efficiency and continual learning. OPSD and &quot;dreaming&quot; may be the keys that let AI learn from deployment rather than from pre-training alone. Dwarkesh Podcast Dwarkesh The next big breakthrough will be AIs learning on the job Continual learning RLVR Sample efficiency OPSD AI training Architectural innovation RLVR (reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards) OPSD (on-policy self-distillation) Dreaming KV cache Sample efficiency\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-26-dwarkesh-ai-的下一个突破-在工作中学习-而非仅靠训练/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://apple.dwarkesh-podcast.workers.dev/art/v1/c3Vic3RhY2s6cG9zdDoyMDM3MDQ1Njg.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">19:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Dwarkesh Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0626</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s next breakthrough isn&#x27;t training — it&#x27;s letting AI learn on the job</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The labs are betting RLVR will generalize into general intelligence, but the real bottlenecks are sample efficiency and continual learning. OPSD and &quot;dreaming&quot; may be the keys that let AI learn from deployment rather than from pre-training alone.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Continual learning</span><span class=\"tag\">RLVR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Disney&#x27;s moat isn&#x27;t the IP, it&#x27;s the flywheel Walt engineered Disney&#x27;s moat is not the IP itself. It is the flywheel Walt built with engineering discipline after art and commerce married inside his head: make high-quality animation, maximise its distribution, feed it into ancillary nodes, then let the whole thing compound for decades. Acquired Acquired The Walt Disney Company IP Strategy Flywheel Effect Animation Industry Long-Term Thinking Vertical Integration Disney Flywheel Multiplane camera Cel animation Pencil test Seven Powers\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-22-acquired-迪士尼飞轮-艺术-商业与工程的百年复利/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/kCB3B2iISM-bCdDu6pysFaFa0p3IYktCnNb8Q5VFycc/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS85MmI3/Mjg0MDI2MWU4ZDc4/M2YyOGZjMzllNjll/ODBlYi5qcGc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">4:31:29</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Acquired</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0622</span></div>\n<h2>Disney&#x27;s moat isn&#x27;t the IP, it&#x27;s the flywheel Walt engineered</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Disney&#x27;s moat is not the IP itself. It is the flywheel Walt built with engineering discipline after art and commerce married inside his head: make high-quality animation, maximise its distribution, feed it into ancillary nodes, then let the whole thing compound for decades.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>17</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>12</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">IP Strategy</span><span class=\"tag\">Flywheel Effect</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\"\n data-hay=\"Mothers Aren&#x27;t Sick, Society Is: How a Depression Diagnosis Moves the Problem Burnout gets misdiagnosed as depression, and the problem is attributed to the individual brain rather than the social environment. A New Zealand study found that new mothers who had someone help with the housework every day for six months almost never developed postpartum depression, yet medication is still the first-line answer. Your Parenting Mojo Your Parenting Mojo Episode Summary 10: Burnout vs Depression: The Mental Load of Mothers Depression diagnosis Maternal burnout Psychiatric drugs Medicalization Social control Postpartum depression Burnout DSM Medicalization Benzodiazepines\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-15-parentmojo-妈妈不是病了-是社会病了-抑郁诊断如何转移问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://artwork.captivate.fm/12802a36-dbca-4912-a62e-cbce5aacddb8/podcast-cover-your-parenting-mojo-03-01-copy.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">18:09</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Your Parenting Mojo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0615</span></div>\n<h2>Mothers Aren&#x27;t Sick, Society Is: How a Depression Diagnosis Moves the Problem</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Burnout gets misdiagnosed as depression, and the problem is attributed to the individual brain rather than the social environment. A New Zealand study found that new mothers who had someone help with the housework every day for six months almost never developed postpartum depression, yet medication is still the first-line answer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Depression diagnosis</span><span class=\"tag\">Maternal burnout</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Lite-version red packets aren&#x27;t growth, they&#x27;re a harvester for the algorithm and monetization Once the demographic dividend was gone, the point of red packets, Lite apps and coupon drops was never growth — it was using monetization and the recommendation algorithm to absorb the traffic. In the AI era paid acquisition is close to useless, and growth goes back to model capability and mindshare marketing. 乱翻书 乱翻书 发券、裂变、极速版，如何用红包设计增长？丨字节跳动 第8集 User growth Lite apps Red-packet virality Coupon drops Spring Festival ops AI acquisition K-factor (viral coefficient) RY1 / RY2 / RY3 (acquisition ROI, gross-margin ROI, net-profit ROI) Red-packet middle platform\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-12-luanfanshu-极速版的本质不是增长-是商业化和算法/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/FvoytLC_DU3W5UAn2k_WBog-CuhI.jpg?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"乱\"><span class=\"dur\">2:59:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">乱翻书</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0612</span></div>\n<h2>Lite-version red packets aren&#x27;t growth, they&#x27;re a harvester for the algorithm and monetization</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Once the demographic dividend was gone, the point of red packets, Lite apps and coupon drops was never growth — it was using monetization and the recommendation algorithm to absorb the traffic. In the AI era paid acquisition is close to useless, and growth goes back to model capability and mindshare marketing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">User growth</span><span class=\"tag\">Lite apps</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\"\n data-hay=\"ADHD Medication Changes Behavior, Not Learning Barkley likens ADHD to diabetes, yet 64% of children move in and out of the diagnostic criteria repeatedly; medication buys compliance without improving learning, the long-term MTA follow-up confirms no academic advantage, and what actually works is small-group differentiated teaching. Your Parenting Mojo Your Parenting Mojo 266: If ADHD Medication Doesn’t Help Kids Learn, What Does? ADHD Child education Drug efficacy Evidence-based teaching Behavioral intervention MTA MTA study crossover design DSM misrecognition\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-01-parentmojo-adhd-药物改得了行为-改不了学习/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://artwork.captivate.fm/12802a36-dbca-4912-a62e-cbce5aacddb8/podcast-cover-your-parenting-mojo-03-01-copy.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">30:41</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Your Parenting Mojo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0601</span></div>\n<h2>ADHD Medication Changes Behavior, Not Learning</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Barkley likens ADHD to diabetes, yet 64% of children move in and out of the diagnostic criteria repeatedly; medication buys compliance without improving learning, the long-term MTA follow-up confirms no academic advantage, and what actually works is small-group differentiated teaching.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">ADHD</span><span class=\"tag\">Child education</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"14,000 cars a year, worth more than Ford: Ferrari sells exclusivity and inclusion at once Ferrari builds only about 14,000 cars a year, yet its market value exceeds Ford&#x27;s. The trick is holding a luxury brand&#x27;s exclusivity and a sports team&#x27;s inclusiveness at the same time: scarcity manufactures the myth, community sustains the loyalty. Acquired Acquired Ferrari Ferrari Luxury goods Scarcity Brand Business model Motor racing Tifosi Classiche Purosangue\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-04-13-acquired-法拉利-卖的不是车-是排他与包容的悖论/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/0QGXNUgszcCY1ANfR29j6wYwABqNDaHjFNi3K5p7ZOw/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS8yYjg2/ZjI2MTRkZGRhNWVl/ZjlkYjA2Zjg2ZWI0/NGVhZS5qcGc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">3:59:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Acquired</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0413</span></div>\n<h2>14,000 cars a year, worth more than Ford: Ferrari sells exclusivity and inclusion at once</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Ferrari builds only about 14,000 cars a year, yet its market value exceeds Ford&#x27;s. The trick is holding a luxury brand&#x27;s exclusivity and a sports team&#x27;s inclusiveness at the same time: scarcity manufactures the myth, community sustains the loyalty.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ferrari</span><span class=\"tag\">Luxury goods</span>\n</div></div></a>"]